---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base
  title="Privacy — ThemePark"
  description="ThemePark collects nothing. All settings stay on your device. No analytics, no network requests, no accounts."
>
  <h1 class="page-title">Privacy</h1>
  <p class="page-meta">Last updated: November 2026</p>

  <div class="card card--prose">
    <p>
      <strong>ThemePark collects nothing.</strong> It has no servers, no analytics, no accounts,
      and makes no network requests of its own. Everything it does — themes, fonts, animation
      settings, per-site profiles — is computed and stored locally in your browser using
      Chrome's storage APIs.
    </p>
    <p>
      The extension reads the pages you visit only to apply the visual settings you chose
      (colors, fonts, motion). It never sends page content, URLs, or usage data anywhere.
      There is no telemetry to opt out of, because there is no telemetry.
    </p>
    <p>
      The website (this one) is static; it sets no cookies and performs no tracking. The
      extension is open source — you can verify all of the above in the
      <a href="https://github.com/D1bakar/Theme-park" rel="noopener">public repository</a>.
    </p>
  </div>
</Base>
